","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/device-enrollment#verify-the-endpoints","content":"Verify the endpoints"},"1010":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/device-enrollment-8","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/device-enrollment","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/device-enrollment#trust-distribution","content":"Trust distribution"},"1011":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/device-enrollment-9","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/device-enrollment","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/device-enrollment#operate-the-dms-inventory","content":"Operate the DMS inventory"},"1012":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/device-enrollment-10","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/device-enrollment","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/device-enrollment#integrate-the-devices","content":"Integrate the devices"},"1013":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/device-enrollment-11","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/device-enrollment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/device-enrollment","content":"A &#x2A;*Device Management Service (DMS)** acts as the registration authority facing a fleet. It receives requests, applies the authentication policy and delegates issuance to the configured CA."},"1014":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/device-enrollment-12","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/device-enrollment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/device-enrollment","content":"Each DMS is an independent operational boundary: it can represent a product line, an environment or a device type with its own CA, authentication rules, distributed trust and renewal window."},"1015":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/device-enrollment-13","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/device-enrollment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/device-enrollment#before-you-begin","content":"Create or import at least one active CA."},"1016":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/device-enrollment-14","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/device-enrollment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/device-enrollmen