/docs/platform/pki/device-enrollment#verify-the-endpoints","content":"From the DMS menu, open &#x2A;*EST (RFC-7030)** and check the base URL and the invocation examples before integrating the firmware."},"1024":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/device-enrollment-22","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/device-enrollment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/device-enrollment#trust-distribution","content":"**Include Lamassu System CA** distributes the TLS certificate of the Lamassu server, useful for *pinning*. It does not represent an issuing CA."},"1025":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/device-enrollment-23","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/device-enrollment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/device-enrollment#trust-distribution","content":"**Include Enrollment CA** adds the authority configured to issue the DMS's identities."},"1026":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/device-enrollment-24","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/device-enrollment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/device-enrollment#trust-distribution","content":"**Managed CAs** lets you include additional authorities the device must consider trusted."},"1027":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/device-enrollment-25","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/device-enrollment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/device-enrollment#operate-the-dms-inventory","content":"**Edit** modifies the DMS policy."},"1028":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/device-enrollment-26","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/device-enrollment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/device-enrollment#operate-the-dms-inventory","content":"**Go to DMS owned devices** opens only the devices of that fleet."},"1029":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/device-enrollment-27","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/device-enrollment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/device-enrollment#operate-the-dms-inventory","content":"**Show/Edit Metadata** manages advanced configuration and integration data."},"1030":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/device-enrollment-28","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/device-enrollment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/device-enrollment#operate-the-dms-inventory","content":"**EST (RFC-7030)** shows the endpoints and examples specific to the DMS."},"1031":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/device-enrollment-29","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/device-enrollment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/device-enrollment#operate-the-dms-inventory","content":"**Delete** removes the DMS and its configuration. The action is irreversible."},"1032":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/device-enrollment-30","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/device-enrollment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/device-enrollment#integrate-the-devices","content":"<Card title=\"EST enrollment\" description=\"Configure authentication, endpoints and flows for firmware.\" href=\"/docs/platform/pki/est-enrollment\" />"},"1033":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/device-enrollment-31","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/device-enrollment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/device-enrollment#integrate-the-devices","content":"<Card title=\"Devices and identities\" description=\"Review statuses, history and operational actions.\" href=\"/docs/platform/pki/device-management\" />"},"1034":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/device-management","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/device-management","type":"page","content":"Devices and identities","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Platform","Operate Lamassu"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/device-management"},"1035":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/device-management-0","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/device-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/device-management","content":"Register devices and control their identities throughout the lifecycle."},"1036":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/device-management-1","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/device-management","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/device-management#device-states","content":"Device states"},"1037":{"id":"/docs