A."},"1621":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management-104","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management#generate-a-csr","content":"Renewing an identity while keeping the same key."},"1622":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management-105","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management#generate-a-csr","content":"When you open the form, it asks for the subject data and the main certificate attributes:"},"1623":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management-106","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management#generate-a-csr","content":"**Common Name (CN)**: main name of the identity."},"1624":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management-107","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management#generate-a-csr","content":"**Organization (O)**: organization or company."},"1625":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management-108","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management#generate-a-csr","content":"**Organizational Unit (OU)**: department or unit."},"1626":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management-109","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management#generate-a-csr","content":"**Country (C)**: two-letter country code."},"1627":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management-110","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management#generate-a-csr","content":"**State / Province (ST)**: state or province."},"1628":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management-111","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management#generate-a-csr","content":"**Locality (L)**: city or locality."},"1629":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management-112","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management#generate-a-csr","content":"**Email Address**: contact email."},"1630":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management-113","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management#generate-a-csr","content":"**Subject Alternative Names (SANs)**: alternative names or identifiers, such as DNS or IP."},"1631":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management-114","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management#generate-a-csr","content":"Once the form is complete, Lamassu generates the CSR and presents it for download or copy."},"1632":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management-115","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management#sign-locally-with-pkcs11","content":"Lamassu also offers specific help for local integrations through **Sign locally with OpenSSL & PKCS11 tools**."},"1633":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management-116","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management#sign-locally-with-pkcs11","content":"This option shows the steps needed to configure the local environment, load the PKCS#11 module and perform signatures with tools like OpenSSL without extracting the private key from the secured environment."},"1634":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp","type":"page","content":"Online validation with OCSP","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Platform","Operate Lamassu"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp"},"1635":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp-0","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp","content":"Check in real time whether a certificate is still valid or has been revoked."},"1636":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp-1","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp#ocsp-service","content":"OCSP service"},"1637":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp-2","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp#how-the-responder-works-in-lamassu","content":"How the responder works in Lamassu"},"1638":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp-3","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp#embedding-in-issued-certificates","content":"Embedding in issued certificates"},"1639":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp-4","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp#http-endpoints","content":"HTTP endpoints"},"1640":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp-5","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp#check-from-the-interface","content":"Check from the interface"},"1641":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp-6","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp#references","content":"References"},"1642":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp-7","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp#ocsp-service","content":"OCSP (Online Certificate Status Protocol) is the mechanism that lets a relying party check, in real time, whether a specific certificate is valid or has been revoked. Instead of downloading a full list of revoked certificates, the client sends a query with the certificate's serial number and receives a signed response with the current status."},"1643":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp-8","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp#ocsp-service","content":"Lamassu integrates its own OCSP responder that serves these queries by consulting the internal certificate database directly. No external component is required."},"1644":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp-9","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp#how-the-responder-works-in-lamassu","content":"When a client requests the status of a certificate, the responder locates the certificate by its serial number and determines its status from the internal record:"},"1645":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp-10","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp#how-the-responder-works-in-lamassu","content":"If the certificate is active, the response indicates `Good`."},"1646":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp-11","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp#how-the-responder-works-in-lamassu","content":"If the certificate has been revoked, the response indicates `Revoked` and includes the revocation timestamp and the RFC 5280 reason code."},"1647":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp-12","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp#how-the-responder-works-in-lamassu","content":"If the serial number is not found or the status is not recognizable, the response indicates `Unknown`."},"1648":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp-13","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp#how-the-responder-works-in-lamassu","content":"The OCSP response is signed by the issuing CA of the queried certificate, using the cryptographic engine associated with that CA. Lamassu does not use a delegated OCSP signing certificate: the CA acts directly as the responder."},"1649":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp-14","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp#how-the-responder-works-in-lamassu","content":"Each response has a validity window of 24 hours, reflected in the response's `thisUpdate` and `nextUpdate` fields. Clients that cache responses must take this window into account when determining how long a response remains valid."},"1650":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp-15","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp#embedding-in-issued-certificates","content":"The OCSP responder URL is automatically embedded in the AIA (*Authority Information Access*) extension of every certificate issued by Lamassu. Clients that verify certificates can read this URL directly from the certificate without additional configuration."},"1651":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp-16","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp#http-endpoints","content":"The responder accepts both formats defined in RFC 6960:"},"1652":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp-17","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp#http-endpoints","content":"`GET /ocsp/{ocsp_request}` includes the OCSP request Base64url-encoded within the URL itself."},"1653":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp-18","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp#http-endpoints","content":"`POST /ocsp` sends the request in the body with `Content-Type: application/ocsp-request`."},"1654":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp-19","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp#http-endpoints","content":"Example query with `curl` using POST:"},"1655":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp-20","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp#http-endpoints","content":"The response has `Content-Type: application/ocsp-response` and contains the OCSP response in DER format."},"1656":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp-21","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp#check-from-the-interface","content":"From the certificates screen of Lamassu you can launch an OCSP request directly against the selected certificate with the **OCSP Check** action. This action shows the status returned by the responder without needing external tools."},"1657":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp-22","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp#references","content":"RFC 6960 - *X.509 Internet Public Key Infrastructure Online Certificate Status Protocol – OCSP*"},"1658":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp-23","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp#references","content":"RFC 5280 - *Internet X.509 Public Key Infrastructure Certificate and Certificate Revocation List (CRL) Profile* (revocation reasons, section 5.3.1)"},"1659":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp-24","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp#references","content":"<Card title=\"CRL service\" href=\"/docs/platform/pki/crl\" />"},"1660":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp-25","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp#references","content":"<Card title=\"Certificate validation\" href=\"/docs/platform/pki/certificate-validation\" />"},"1661":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview","type":"page","content":"Lamassu IoT Platform","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Platform"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/overview"},"1662":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview-0","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/overview","content":"Manage PKI and digital identities for your devices from a single platform."},"1663":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview-1","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/overview#start-here","content":"Start here"},"1664":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview-2","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/overview#architecture-at-a-glance","content":"Architecture at a glance"},"1665":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview-3","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/overview#core-capabilities","content":"Core capabilities"},"1666":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview-4","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/overview#build-your-trust-hierarchy","content":"Build your trust hierarchy"},"1667":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview-5","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/overview#protect-cryptographic-keys","content":"Protect cryptographic keys"},"1668":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview-6","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/overview#issue-and-control-certificates","content":"Issue and control certificates"},"1669":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview-7","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/overview#automate-device-identities","content":"Automate device identities"},"1670":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview-8","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/overview#publish-validation-status","content":"Publish validation status"},"1671":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview-9","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/overview#react-to-events","content":"React to events"},"1672":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview-10","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/overview#choose-your-path","content":"Choose your path"},"1673":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview-11","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/overview#operational-reference","content":"Operational reference"},"1674":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview-12","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/overview","content":"Lamassu IoT centralizes the issuance, distribution, renewal and revocation of X.509 identities for connected devices. You can build a private PKI, protect its keys and automate the enrollment of a fleet without losing visibility into every certificate."},"1675":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview-13","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/overview#start-here","content":"<Card title=\"Get started\" description=\"Create a CA, issue a certificate and register your first device.\" href=\"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview\" />"},"1676":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview-14","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/overview#start-here","content":"<Card title=\"How Lamassu works\" description=\"Build the mental model of authorities, keys, identities and validation.\" href=\"/docs/platform/pki/concepts/overview\" />"},"1677":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview-15","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/overview#architecture-at-a-glance","content":"Lamassu runs as a set of services on Kubernetes, backed by PostgreSQL, RabbitMQ and an OIDC provider. Hover a component to trace its connections, or see the platform architecture chapter for the low-level, per-service view."},"1678":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview-16","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/overview#build-your-trust-hierarchy","content":"Create root and intermediate authorities or import an existing PKI. Define which authority can issue each identity and keep the full chain of trust."},"1679":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview-17","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/overview#protect-cryptographic-keys","content":"Generate and safeguard keys using software engines, PKCS#11 HSMs or cloud services. Lamassu decouples operations from the physical location of the key."},"1680":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview-18","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/overview#issue-and-control-certificates","content":"Issue certificates from the console or from a CSR, check their status and revoke them when they stop being trustworthy."},"1681":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview-19","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/overview#automate-device-identities","content":"Define enrollment policies with a Device Management Service (DMS) and let devices request or renew their identity through EST."},"1682":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview-20","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/overview#publish-validation-status","content":"Offer online validation through OCSP and distribute CRLs for consumers that need to check certificates offline."},"1683":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview-21","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/overview#react-to-events","content":"Subscribe to lifecycle changes and send notifications by email, Microsoft Teams or webhooks."},"1684":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview-22","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/overview#choose-your-path","content":"<Card title=\"I administer the PKI\" description=\"Configure engines, authorities, issuance and validation.\" href=\"/docs/platform/pki/key-management\" />"},"1685":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview-23","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/overview#choose-your-path","content":"<Card title=\"I integrate a device\" description=\"Configure the DMS and use EST to obtain an identity.\" href=\"/docs/platform/pki/device-enrollment\" />"},"1686":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview-24","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/overview#choose-your-path","content":"<Card title=\"I operate the platform\" description=\"Deploy Lamassu and prepare its dependencies.\" href=\"/docs/deployment/overview\" />"},"1687":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview-25","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/overview#choose-your-path","content":"<Card title=\"I integrate another system\" description=\"Connect Lamassu with AWS IoT Core and other destinations.\" href=\"/docs/platform/pki/integrations/aws-iot-core\" />"},"1688":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview-26","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/overview#operational-reference","content":"<Card title=\"Certificate profiles\" description=\"Turn issuance policy into reusable constraints.\" href=\"/docs/platform/pki/certificate-profiles\" />"},"1689":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview-27","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/overview#operational-reference","content":"<Card title=\"Hierarchy and rotation\" description=\"Replace CA certificates or keys without breaking trust.\" href=\"/docs/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation\" />"},"1690":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview-28","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/overview#operational-reference","content":"<Card title=\"Access control\" description=\"Configure principals, policies and the first administrator.\" href=\"/docs/platform/pki/access-control\" />"},"1691":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview-29","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/overview#operational-reference","content":"<Card title=\"Troubleshooting\" description=\"Diagnose the Gateway, services, issuance and enrollment.\" href=\"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting\" />"},"1692":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority","type":"page","content":"Create your first CA","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Platform","Getting started"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority"},"1693":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority-0","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority","content":"Create a root authority and check that it is ready to issue certificates."},"1694":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority-1","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority#before-you-begin","content":"Before you begin"},"1695":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority-2","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority#open-the-creation-wizard","content":"Open the creation wizard"},"1696":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority-3","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority#select-the-key","content":"Select the key"},"1697":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority-4","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority#define-the-authority","content":"Define the authority"},"1698":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority-5","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority#review-and-create-the-ca","content":"Review and create the CA"},"1699":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority-6","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority#verify-the-result","content":"Verify the result"},"1700":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority-7","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority#next-step","content":"Next step"},"1701":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority-8","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority","content":"In this quickstart you will create a root certification authority with a new key pair. When you finish you will have an active CA that you can use in the next quickstart."},"1702":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority-9","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority#before-you-begin","content":"Console access with permissions to manage authorities."},"1703":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority-10","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority#before-you-begin","content":"At least one cryptographic engine available."},"1704":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority-11","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority#before-you-begin","content":"A name that identifies the purpose of the CA, for example `Acme Device Root CA`."},"1705":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority-12","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority#before-you-begin","content":"A root CA is self-signed and acts as the anchor of trust. For production it is usually preferable to keep the root more protected and issue from an intermediate CA."},"1706":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority-13","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority#open-the-creation-wizard","content":"In the side menu, open **Certification Authorities** and select **Create New CA**."},"1707":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority-14","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority#open-the-creation-wizard","content":"Choose to create a CA with a new key pair. If you already have the key in the KMS, use &#x2A;*Create New CA (Existing Key)**."},"1708":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority-15","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority#select-the-key","content":"Choose the cryptographic engine that will keep the key and configure the algorithm. For a first CA you can use **EC P-384**, as long as it is compatible with your consumers."},"1709":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority-16","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority#select-the-key","content":"The private key will remain under the control of the selected engine."},"1710":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority-17","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority#define-the-authority","content":"Select **Root CA** and complete:"},"1711":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority-18","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority#define-the-authority","content":"**CA Name**: a unique, recognizable name."},"1712":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority-19","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority#define-the-authority","content":"**Subject**: at least the organization and country that will identify the authority."},"1713":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority-20","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority#define-the-authority","content":"**CA Certificate Expiration**: a validity longer than that of the certificates it will issue."},"1714":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority-21","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority#define-the-authority","content":"**Default End-Entity Certificate Issuance Expiration**: the default validity of end-entity certificates."},"1715":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority-22","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority#define-the-authority","content":"The CA name will be used as the certificate's `Common Name`."},"1716":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority-23","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority#review-and-create-the-ca","content":"Check the algorithm, subject and dates before confirming. These values define the anchor of trust and should not be chosen as throwaway test data in a production environment."},"1717":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority-24","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority#verify-the-result","content":"Open the new CA from the list. It should appear active and show its PEM certificate, the expiration date and the **Issued Certificates** tab."},"1718":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority-25","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority#next-step","content":"Use the authority to issue your first certificate, or see the full authorities guide to create an intermediate CA, import a CA or define advanced profiles."},"1719":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","type":"page","content":"Issue your first certificate","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Platform","Getting started"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate"},"1720":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-0","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","content":"Issue an X.509 identity from the console and verify the result."},"1721":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-1","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#before-you-begin","content":"Before you begin"},"1722":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-2","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#start-the-issuance","content":"Start the issuance"},"1723":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-3","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#choose-the-method","content":"Choose the method"},"1724":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-4","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#identify-the-certificate","content":"Identify the certificate"},"1725":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-5","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#configure-key-and-uses","content":"Configure key and uses"},"1726":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-6","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#issue-and-download","content":"Issue and download"},"1727":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-7","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#verify-the-result","content":"Verify the result"},"1728":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-8","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#next-step","content":"Next step"},"1729":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-9","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","content":"In this quickstart Lamassu will generate the key and the CSR in the browser, and the CA will issue the certificate. When you finish you will download the certificate and its private key."},"1730":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-10","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#before-you-begin","content":"An active CA with permission to issue certificates."},"1731":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-11","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#before-you-begin","content":"A name for the identity, for example `device-001.example.internal`."},"1732":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-12","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#before-you-begin","content":"A safe place to keep the downloaded private key."},"1733":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-13","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#before-you-begin","content":"In this flow the key is generated in the browser and Lamassu does not store it. Download it and protect it before closing the operation result."},"1734":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-14","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#start-the-issuance","content":"Open the CA created in the previous quickstart, go to **Issued Certificates** and select **Issue New**."},"1735":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-15","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#choose-the-method","content":"Select **Generate Key & CSR in Browser**. Use **Upload Existing CSR** when the private key must be generated and kept on the target system."},"1736":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-16","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#identify-the-certificate","content":"Enter the `Common Name` and, if applicable, the organization, organizational unit and location. Add SANs for each DNS name, IP address, email or URI the identity will be validated with."},"1737":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-17","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#configure-key-and-uses","content":"Choose RSA or ECDSA, define the validity and select the key usages. For a device identity that uses mTLS, enable **Digital Signature** and **Client Authentication**."},"1738":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-18","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#configure-key-and-uses","content":"The validity cannot exceed the expiration date of the issuing CA."},"1739":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-19","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#issue-and-download","content":"Confirm the issuance and immediately download the certificate and the private key in PEM format."},"1740":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-20","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#verify-the-result","content":"The certificate should appear in **Issued Certificates** with an active status. Check its subject, SANs, issuer, usages and validity period."},"1741":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-21","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#next-step","content":"Register your first device to associate the identity with a managed entity, or see certificate management."},"1742":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview","type":"page","content":"Get started","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Platform","Getting started"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview"},"1743":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview-0","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview","content":"Get a first result with Lamassu and continue from a working base."},"1744":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview-1","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview#recommended-path","content":"Recommended path"},"1745":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview-2","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview#before-you-begin","content":"Before you begin"},"1746":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview-3","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview","content":"The quickstarts take you from a prepared instance to an active device identity. Each guide produces a verifiable result and links the detailed explanation when you need to go deeper."},"1747":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview-4","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview#recommended-path","content":"<Card title=\"1. Create your first CA\" description=\"Establish a root of trust capable of issuing certificates.\" href=\"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority\" />"},"1748":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview-5","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview#recommended-path","content":"<Card title=\"2. Issue a certificate\" description=\"Create an X.509 identity and verify its contents.\" href=\"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate\" />"},"1749":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview-6","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview#recommended-path","content":"<Card title=\"3. Register a device\" description=\"Add a device and assign it its first identity.\" href=\"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/register-device\" />"},"1750":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview-7","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview#before-you-begin","content":"You need access to the Lamassu IoT console and permissions to administer keys, authorities and devices. The instance must have at least one cryptographic engine configured."},"1751":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview-8","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview#before-you-begin","content":"If you don't have an instance yet, first choose a deployment model."},"1752":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/register-device","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/register-device","type":"page","content":"Register your first device","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Platform","Getting started"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/register-device"},"1753":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/register-device-0","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/register-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/register-device","content":"Add a device to Lamassu and assign it an active identity."},"1754":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/register-device-1","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/register-device","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/register-device#before-you-begin","content":"Before you begin"},"1755":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/register-device-2","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/register-device","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/register-device#register-the-device","content":"Register the device"},"1756":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/register-device-3","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/register-device","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/register-device#check-the-initial-status","content":"Check the initial status"},"1757":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/register-device-4","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/register-device","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/register-device#assign-an-identity","content":"Assign an identity"},"1758":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/register-device-5","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/register-device","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/register-device#verify-the-device","content":"Verify the device"},"1759":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/register-device-6","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/register-device","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/register-device#automate-the-next-device","content":"Automate the next device"},"1760":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/register-device-7","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/register-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/register-device","content":"In this quickstart you will manually register a device and assign it its first certificate. It is the shortest path to understanding how Lamassu relates a physical entity to its identity history."},"1761":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/register-device-8","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/register-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/register-device#before-you-begin","content":"A configured DMS."},"1762":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/register-device-9","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/register-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/register-device#before-you-begin","content":"A CA associated with the DMS."},"1763":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/register-device-10","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/register-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/register-device#before-you-begin","content":"A unique identifier for the device."},"1764":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/register-device-11","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/register-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/register-device#register-the-device","content":"Open **Managed Devices**, select the action to register a device and complete:"},"1765":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/register-device-12","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/register-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/register-device#register-the-device","content":"**Device ID**: unique identifier of the device."},"1766":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/register-device-13","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/register-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/register-device#register-the-device","content":"**Registration Authority**: the DMS that will apply the enrollment policies."},"1767":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/register-device-14","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/register-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/register-device#register-the-device","content":"**Icon** and **Tags**: optional classification to locate it later."},"1768":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/register-device-15","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/register-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/register-device#check-the-initial-status","content":"Open the newly created device. It should appear with status **No Identity**: it exists in the inventory but does not yet have an associated certificate."},"1769":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/register-device-16","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/register-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/register-device#assign-an-identity","content":"Select **Assign Identity**. Lamassu will search for active certificates whose `Common Name` matches the `Device ID`."},"1770":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/register-device-17","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/register-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/register-device#assign-an-identity","content":"Select an existing certificate or use **Issue New Instead** to issue one from a CA linked to the DMS."},"1771":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/register-device-18","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/register-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/register-device#verify-the-device","content":"After confirming, the status should change to **Active**. Review **Certificate History** to check the associated identity and **Device Event Timeline** to see the assignment event."},"1772":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/register-device-19","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/register-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/register-device#automate-the-next-device","content":"Manual registration helps you understand the model, but a fleet should use automated enrollment. Continue with Device Management Service and the EST integration."},"1773":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting","type":"page","content":"Troubleshooting","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Platform","Administer Lamassu"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting"},"1774":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting-0","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting","content":"Diagnose access, health, issuance, enrollment and dependencies in a Lamassu deployment."},"1775":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting-1","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting#diagnostic-sequence","content":"Diagnostic sequence"},"1776":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting-2","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting#reproduce-a-single-operation","content":"Reproduce a single operation"},"1777":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting-3","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting#separate-client-gateway-and-service","content":"Separate client, Gateway and service"},"1778":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting-4","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting#review-kubernetes-status","content":"Review Kubernetes status"},"1779":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting-5","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting#query-the-affected-service","content":"Query the affected service"},"1780":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting-6","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting#validate-the-result-from-outside","content":"Validate the result from outside"},"1781":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting-7","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting#minimal-evidence-collection","content":"Minimal evidence collection"},"1782":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting-8","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting#i-cannot-sign-in","content":"I cannot sign in"},"1783":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting-9","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting#everything-returns-403-or-5xx","content":"Everything returns 403 or 5xx"},"1784":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting-10","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting#a-pod-is-not-ready","content":"A pod is not Ready"},"1785":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting-11","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting#issuance-fails","content":"Issuance fails"},"1786":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting-12","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting#est-enrollment-fails","content":"EST enrollment fails"},"1787":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting-13","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting#ocsp-or-crl-do-not-reflect-a-change","content":"OCSP or CRL do not reflect a change"},"1788":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting-14","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting#events-are-not-arriving","content":"Events are not arriving"},"1789":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting-15","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting#observability","content":"Observability"},"1790":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting-16","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting","content":"Start by locating the failing layer. A Gateway response, an unready pod and a rejected issuance can look like the same problem from the console, but they require different evidence."},"1791":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting-17","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting#reproduce-a-single-operation","content":"Note the time in UTC, user or principal, resource, endpoint and result. Avoid repeating a destructive action such as revocation or deletion."},"1792":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting-18","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting#separate-client-gateway-and-service","content":"Check the HTTP status. A 401 points to authentication; a 403, to authorization; a 404, to route or resource; a 5xx, to the service or a dependency."},"1793":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting-19","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting#review-kubernetes-status","content":"Locate unready pods, restarts, recent events and the state of the release."},"1794":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting-20","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting#query-the-affected-service","content":"Review its /health endpoint and its logs in the same time window. Then follow the indicated dependency: PostgreSQL, RabbitMQ, the OIDC provider or the cryptographic engine."},"1795":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting-21","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting#validate-the-result-from-outside","content":"For PKI, check the certificate, the chain, OCSP or CRL with the same type of client production uses."},"1796":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting-22","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting#minimal-evidence-collection","content":"Replace the placeholders with your real release, namespace and deployment."},"1797":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting-23","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting#minimal-evidence-collection","content":"Also run the chart's connectivity test:"},"1798":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting-24","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting#minimal-evidence-collection","content":"The test checks the health of CA, DMS Manager, Device Manager and VA, and verifies that the UI returns HTML. A passing test confirms basic connectivity, not a full issuance flow."},"1799":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting-25","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting#minimal-evidence-collection","content":"The chart's services expose startup, readiness and liveness probes over /health. A pod can be running but receive no traffic if the readiness probe fails."},"1800":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting-26","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting#i-cannot-sign-in","content":"If you receive a 401:"},"1801":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting-27","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting#i-cannot-sign-in","content":"check that the UI's OIDC authority is reachable from the browser;"},"1802":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting-28","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting#i-cannot-sign-in","content":"verify issuer, audience and expiration of the token;"},"1803":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting-29","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting#i-cannot-sign-in","content":"confirm the Gateway can fetch the keys from the JWKS URI;"},"1804":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting-30","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting#i-cannot-sign-in","content":"check that the provider's public and internal routes point to the same realm."},"1805":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting-31","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting#i-cannot-sign-in","content":"If login succeeds but the APIs return 403:"},"1806":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting-32","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting#i-cannot-sign-in","content":"inspect the token's real claims;"},"1807":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting-33","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting#i-cannot-sign-in","content":"confirm they match an active principal;"},"1808":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting-34","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting#i-cannot-sign-in","content":"review the policies granted to that principal;"},"1809":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting-35","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting#i-cannot-sign-in","content":"verify that authz reaches PostgreSQL and its JWKS."},"1810":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting-36","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting#i-cannot-sign-in","content":"On a fresh installation, confirm the migration Job finished. That Job creates schemas, migrates authz, preloads policies and provisions the principals defined in services.authz.bootstrap."},"1811":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting-37","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting#everything-returns-403-or-5xx","content":"External authorization fails closed by default. If authz is unavailable, protected routes are blocked."},"1812":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting-38","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting#everything-returns-403-or-5xx","content":"Locate the authz pod and Service."},"1813":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting-39","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting#everything-returns-403-or-5xx","content":"Check /health, logs and its database connection."},"1814":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting-40","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting#everything-returns-403-or-5xx","content":"Verify the DNS and port configured in externalAuthorization."},"1815":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting-41","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting#everything-returns-403-or-5xx","content":"Check the check route is /v1/ext\\_authz/check."},"1816":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting-42","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting#everything-returns-403-or-5xx","content":"Do not switch to failOpen: true as a permanent workaround: it would allow traffic without authorization during the outage."},"1817":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/troublesh