d/networking#qué-ocurre-si-necesitas-tres-gateways","content":"Solo separación lógica; cada listener necesita una tupla única de puerto, protocolo y hostname"},"288":{"id":"/docs/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking-53","page_id":"/docs/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking#qué-ocurre-si-necesitas-tres-gateways","content":"Tres Services `LoadBalancer` independientes no pueden reservar a la vez los mismos puertos 80 y 443 mediante K3s ServiceLB. Usa un Gateway compartido, asigna VIP distintas con otro balanceador o utiliza puertos diferentes."},"289":{"id":"/docs/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking-54","page_id":"/docs/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking#qué-ocurre-si-necesitas-tres-gateways","content":"Envoy Gateway provisiona normalmente un proxy fleet por `Gateway`. Su modo merged Gateway puede compartir un fleet y una dirección, pero no es un cambio directo para varias releases de Lamassu: los listeners generados usan los mismos puertos y protocolos sin hostnames distintos, por lo que entran en conflicto salvo que personalices el diseño."},"290":{"id":"/docs/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking-55","page_id":"/docs/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking#qué-ocurre-si-necesitas-tres-gateways","content":"Usa un front door con SNI solo cuando los Gateways internos deban mantener políticas TLS o mTLS independientes:"},"291":{"id":"/docs/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking-56","page_id":"/docs/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking#qué-ocurre-si-necesitas-tres-gateways","content":"Esto requiere hostnames SNI distintos y configuración de red externa al chart de Lamassu."},"292":{"id":"/docs/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking-57","page_id":"/docs/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking#guía-de-decisión","content":"Si un Gateway puede gestionar TLS y el enrutamiento, usa el valor predeterminado del chart."},"293":{"id":"/docs/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking-58","page_id":"/docs/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking#guía-de-decisión","content":"Si los Gateways necesitan políticas independientes y puedes asignar IP, usa una VIP por Gateway."},"294":{"id":"/docs/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking-59","page_id":"/docs/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking#guía-de-decisión","content":"Si solo necesitas separar los recursos Kubernetes, evalúa merged Gateway y usa tuplas de listener únicas."},"295":{"id":"/docs/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking-60","page_id":"/docs/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking#guía-de-decisión","content":"Si los data planes y la terminación TLS deben ser independientes detrás de una IP, añade un front door con TLS passthrough y SNI."},"296":{"id":"/docs/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking-61","page_id":"/docs/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking#guía-de-decisión","content":"Si nada de lo anterior es posible, usa puertos externos distintos o cambia el diseño de red."},"297":{"id":"/docs/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking-62","page_id":"/docs/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking#verifica-la-ruta-de-tráfico","content":"Comprueba, en orden:"},"298":{"id":"/docs/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking-63","page_id":"/docs/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking#verifica-la-ruta-de-tráfico","content":"El `Gateway` muestra `Accepted=True` y `Programmed=True`."},"299":{"id":"/docs/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking-64","page_id":"/docs/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking#verifica-la-ruta-de-tráfico","content":"Su estado contiene la dirección esperada."},"300":{"id":"/docs/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking-65","page_id":"/docs/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking#verifica-la-ruta-de-tráfico","content":"El Service `LoadBalancer` generado tiene una dirección externa utilizable."},"301":{"id":"/docs/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking-66","page_id":"/docs/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking#verifica-la-ruta-de-tráfico","content":"El puerto 443 de esa dirección es accesible desde la red del cliente."},"302":{"id":"/docs/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking-67","page_id":"/docs/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking#verifica-la-ruta-de-tráfico","content":"DNS resuelve al endpoint accesible externamente."},"303":{"id":"/docs/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking-68","page_id":"/docs/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking#verifica-la-ruta-de-tráfico","content":"El certificado contiene el nombre DNS o la IP usada por el cliente."},"304":{"id":"/docs/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking-69","page_id":"/docs/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking#verifica-la-ruta-de-tráfico","content":"Gateway API trata las direcciones como estado deseado que el controlador puede asignar o rechazar; consulta la introducción a Gateway API para conocer el modelo."},"305":{"id":"/docs/es/deployment/self-hosted/overview","page_id":"/docs/es/deployment/self-host